  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...A warming trend and\ndrying trend will set in come Tuesday as the low exits to the \neast. Our far eastern zones may end up on the periphery of the \nwrap around precipitation associated with the low, leading to a \n20-40% chance of precipitation Tuesday morning; generally south \nand east of Mountain Home. Tuesday and Wednesday afternoons will\nremain breezy as the low exits. Beyond Tuesday, a warming trend\nwill set in through the start of the weekend with dry \nconditions. This is thanks to a ridge that will build in over \nthe West Coast before eventually shifting to be over the Great \nBasin. Temperatures will start out right around normal Tuesday \nbefore increasing to around 5-10 degrees above normal by Friday.",
